ror":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Framework:** compare total cost, time to market and control against expected fund count and asset trajectory.\n\n**Series trust (white-label):**\n- Existing board, CCO, auditor, administrator, custodian and exemptive/Rule 6c-11 infrastructure enable faster, cheaper launches.\n- Costs are mostly per-fund or asset-based, often with minimums, and can become expensive at scale.\n- **Control trade-off:** the platform's board and adviser oversee you, can terminate or replace you, and shape providers, policies and timing. Your brand may share governance risk with unrelated funds.\n\n**Own trust:**\n- Full control over board composition, vendors and future lineup.\n- Requires substantial upfront legal, board and CCO costs, longer setup, and fixed costs a single fund must bear.\n\n**Deciding factors:** realistic AUM and break-even, plans for more funds, strategy complexity, distribution relationships and tolerance for oversight.\n\nFor most single-fund, budget-limited sponsors, a series trust is a reasonable start. Negotiate exit and reorganization terms upfront, and get current fee quotes and legal advice.","ttft_ms":1832,"type":"result","duration_ms":4097,"uuid":"5c127697-9a39-4f74-8bbb-a4b8c712f074","ttft_stream_ms":1386,"time_to_request_ms":70,"first_content_frame_ms":1386,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
